IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il37-nouns`
IMPORT `il37-committee`

-- Basic Law: The Judiciary (חוק־יסוד: השפיטה), the Judicial Selection Committee, THE SEAT LAYER. Row IL-37.
--
-- SEAT: a person the committee's rules are applied to: a candidate whom the committee has chosen (or declined to choose) as a judge, and a judge whom the committee is asked to remove.
-- The committee, the Minister of Justice, the Knesset and the Court have no seat here. Every question takes plain facts the person could state (who voted for them, how many voted,
-- who proposed it), and calls the rule already encoded in il37-committee.l4; no rule is restated. Nothing here is new law.
-- A BOOLEAN answers "on these facts, yes or no under the text"; the rules for the committee from the 26th Knesset are the ones the first question applies.

§ `The questions of a candidate for judicial office, and of a judge`

§§ `Was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got? (s 4(d) to (f))`

-- Plain inputs: one BOOLEAN per seat, in the order of the committee from the 26th Knesset. The last two seats are the public representatives; where the coalition factions number
-- more than 80 Knesset members, the two are the ones the Knesset as a whole chose (s 4(f)(2)), and the question about the 80 Knesset members says which.
@export Was the committee's choice of me as a judge valid, under the text from the 26th Knesset, on the votes it got?
GIVEN `the court I was chosen for is the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the committee choosing you as a judge of the Supreme Court (yes) or of a district or magistrates' court (no)?
      `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the factions of the coalition number more than 80 Knesset members when the committee voted?
      `the President of the Supreme Court voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the President of the Supreme Court vote for you?
      `the first other justice voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the first of the two other Supreme Court justices on the committee vote for you?
      `the second other justice voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the second of the two other Supreme Court justices on the committee vote for you?
      `the Minister of Justice voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister of Justice vote for you?
      `the other minister voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the other minister on the committee vote for you?
      `the coalition Knesset member voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Knesset member of the coalition factions vote for you?
      `the opposition Knesset member voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Knesset member of the opposition factions vote for you?
      `the first public representative voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the public representative chosen by the coalition Knesset members (or, where the coalition has more than 80, the first one the Knesset chose) vote for you?
      `the second public representative voted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the public representative chosen by the opposition Knesset members (or, where the coalition has more than 80, the second one the Knesset chose) vote for you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got` MEANS
    `the majority of section 4 is met` tally kind `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            IF `the court I was chosen for is the Supreme Court`
            THEN `the election of a judge of the Supreme Court`
            ELSE `the election of a judge of a court other than the Supreme Court`
        tally MEANS
            LIST (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the President of the Supreme Court`, `the President of the Supreme Court voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, `the first other justice voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, `the second other justice voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Minister of Justice`, `the Minister of Justice voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another minister whom the Government names`, `the other minister voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`, `the coalition Knesset member voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the opposition factions`, `the opposition Knesset member voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF (IF `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members` THEN `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose` ELSE `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose`), `the first public representative voted for me`),
                 (`A member serving on the committee` OF (IF `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members` THEN `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose` ELSE `the public representative whom the opposition Knesset members chose`), `the second public representative voted for me`)

§§ `Can the committee end my term as a judge on the votes it got? (s 7(4))`

-- The text of s 7(4) is the same before and after the 26th Knesset; in the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 s 3 the committee's other decisions need all the members serving.
@export Can the committee end my term as a judge on the votes it got?
GIVEN `who proposed it` IS A `Who proposes to end a judge's term` @desc Who proposed to the committee that your term be ended: the Minister of Justice as chair, the Commissioner for Complaints against Judges, the President of the Supreme Court, or someone else?
      `which text applies on the day of the vote` IS A `A vintage of the committee rule` @desc Which applies on the day of the vote: the text before the 26th Knesset, the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3, or the text from the 26th Knesset?
      `the number of members serving` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members were serving on the committee on the day of the vote?
      `the number who voted to end my term` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members voted to end your term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`can the committee end my term on the votes it got` MEANS
    `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `who proposed it` (`a tally of so many serving, so many in favour` `the number of members serving` `the number who voted to end my term`) `which text applies on the day of the vote`

-- Helper, not a question: a tally of members serving of whom so many vote in favour. Only the count matters to s 7(4), so each is seated as the Minister of Justice.
GIVEN serving IS A NUMBER
      `in favour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
`a tally of so many serving, so many in favour` MEANS
    IF serving AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Minister of Justice`, (`in favour` GREATER THAN 0))
         FOLLOWED BY `a tally of so many serving, so many in favour` (serving MINUS 1) (`in favour` MINUS 1)
